    (
        6,
        24,
        "",
        "Yahweh bless you, and keep you",
        "word",
        "Hebrew",
        "Hebrew",
        "<strong>Birkat Kohanim — the Priestly Blessing.</strong> The oldest biblical text ever recovered archaeologically: two tiny silver scrolls from the Ketef Hinnom burial chamber (7th c. BCE, predating the Dead Sea Scrolls by ~400 years) bear an abbreviated form of this blessing. Three escalating lines, three names of YHWH, three rising syllables in Hebrew (3, 5, 7 words). Still pronounced over the congregation in synagogues every morning and on Jewish festivals; the Christian liturgy adapts it under various names.",
        "User original",
    ),
