    # ---- ch 10 ----
    (
        10,
        35,
        "",
        "Rise up, Yahweh",
        "source",
        "Variant",
        "Variant",
        "<strong>The inverted nuns (<em>נון</em> <em>מנוזרת</em>).</strong> In the Masoretic text, verses 35–36 are bracketed by two inverted Hebrew letter <em>nun</em>s — one of the rarest scribal phenomena in the entire Hebrew Bible. The Talmud (<em>Shabbat</em> 115b–116a) records two interpretations: that this short hymn is misplaced and originally belonged elsewhere; or that it constitutes a separate “book” of the Torah, making seven books rather than five. Either way, the brackets are a self-aware textual marker — the scribes signaling that the text in their hands is provisional. Few passages in scripture wear their textual history so visibly.",
        "User paraphrase; references Talmud",
    ),
