    (
        15,
        32,
        "",
        "gathering sticks on the Sabbath",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The stick-gatherer.</strong> One of the few biblical narratives where capital punishment is imposed for Sabbath violation. The narrative is uneasy with itself: the people <em>didn’t know what to do with him</em> (15:34). The execution is by stoning outside the camp (15:36) — the same procedure later applied in Lev 24 (the blasphemer) and forming the procedural template for Stephen’s death in Acts 7. Rabbinic tradition uses this passage to develop the principle that ignorance of the law does not exempt — but neither does the text show enthusiasm for the verdict.",
        "User original",
    ),
