        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>ASHES</strong> The ashes of a red heifer burned entire (Numbers 19:5) when sprinkled on the unclean made them ceremonially clean (Hebrews 9:13). To cover the head with ashes was a token of self-abhorrence and humiliation (2 Samuel 13:19; Esther 4:3; Jeremiah 6:26, etc.). To feed on ashes (Isaiah 44:20), means to seek that which will prove to be vain and unsatisfactory, and hence it denotes the unsatisfactory nature of idol-worship. (Comp. Hos. 12:1).",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
