    (
        20,
        12,
        "",
        "you didn’t believe in me",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Why is Moses barred from the land?</strong> The text itself is famously elliptical. Moses is told to <em>speak</em> to the rock (20:8); he <em>strikes</em> it twice (20:11) and adds an angry word (“must we bring water for you?”). Theories on what exactly disqualified him: striking instead of speaking; striking twice rather than once; the angry rhetorical question implying he and Aaron themselves produce the water; doubting the miracle would happen at all; pre-existing faithlessness now coming to a head. The rabbis count at least eight rabbinic explanations. The narrative effect, however, is unambiguous: even Moses dies outside the land. The covenant exceeds any individual.",
        "User original",
    ),
