        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>JESHIMON</strong> the waste, probably some high waste land to the south of the Dead Sea (Numbers 21:20; 23:28; 1 Samuel 23:19, 24); or rather not a proper name at all, but simply “the waste” or “wilderness,” the district on which the plateau of Ziph (q.v.) looks down.",
