    (
        25,
        1,
        "",
        "play the prostitute with the daughters of Moab",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The Baal Peor incident.</strong> Israel’s sin at Shittim — sexual congress with Moabite women, syncretistic worship of <em>Baal Peor</em> — is the wilderness generation’s last apostasy before entering the land. The episode is referenced repeatedly later as paradigmatic: Hosea 9:10, Psalm 106:28–31, Deuteronomy 4:3. Phinehas’s zealous execution (25:7–8) earns him an everlasting priesthood — an ambivalent passage that has been used in subsequent eras both to commend and to critique violent zeal in religious cause. The 24,000 dead (25:9) is the highest casualty count in the wilderness narrative.",
        "User original",
    ),
