        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>ABEL-SHITTIM</strong> meadow of the acacias, frequently called simply “Shittim” (Numbers 25:1; Joshua 2:1; Micah 6:5), a place on the east of Jordan, in the plain of Moab, nearly opposite Jericho. It was the forty-second encampment of the Israelites, their last resting-place before they crossed the Jordan (Numbers 33:49; 22:1; 26:3; 31:12; comp. 25:1; 31:16).",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
